<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of February 11 in the July-to-June 1996/97 campaign, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>On February 13, the EU also granted exports of 115,500 tonnes of soft wheat, 180,000 tonnes of barley, 1,000 tonnes of rye, 5,500 tonnes of durum and 10,000 tonnes of maize.</p>
<p>Figures ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			     1Jul96 to 11Feb97     1Jul95 to 11Feb96</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  6,950     154     785    4,505	1,157</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    3,987     115	10    3,465	   13</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		246	63	 -	393	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   98	89	 -	110	    -</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	305	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   13		   -	 76	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT   11,294     128     795    8,854	1,170</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	  113		 346	 17	  853</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	   295     894	 0	 33	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   -	 68	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     409     347     346	118	  853</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	    11,703     130   1,141    8,972	2,023</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)     4,083     328	31    1,244	  159</p>
<p>  Malt (4)	     2,658     121	 0    2,191	    0</p>
<p>  Donations		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL BARLEY	  6,741     196	31    3,435	  159</p>
<p>  Maize (grain)	  127   2,117     299	  6	2,299</p>
<p>  Food aid		  11		   -	 40	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL MAIZE	     138     300     299	 46	2,299</p>
<p>  Rye (grain)	    699	56	 3    1,247	   33</p>
<p>  Rye flour (5)	    0		   0	  0	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (5)	    0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL RYE		 699	56	 3    1,247	   33</p>
<p> OATS			377     465	 1	 81	    1</p>
<p>  Sorghum (grain)	  0		   5	  0	  902</p>
<p>  Food aid		   0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SORGHUM	     0		   5	  0	  902</p>
<p>OTHER GRAINS</p>
<p>Buckwheat, Millet,</p>
<p>   Triticale		 1		 152	  1	   88</p>
<p> TOTAL GRAIN	  19,659     143   1,632   13,782	5,505</p>
<p>Note -- (1) column shows this year's exports expressed as a percentage of last year's exports, not as a percentage change (2) wheat equivalent (3) durum equivalent (4) barley equivalent (5) rye equivalent.</p>
